test ops::rns_fhe::tests::test_mul_dual_public_with_mod_switch ... ignored, RETIRED MECHANISM: asserts that mul_dual_public auto-drops the last prime ('primes after switch', ct6_deep.c0.main.len()) and that depth-2 decrypts only because that level was spent ('=== MODULUS SWITCHING SUCCESS ==='). This substrate does not implement modulus switching. Exact division in residue space (K-Elimination for gcd(d,M)=1, Fused Piggyback Division otherwise) divides the ciphertext value by d WITHOUT moving the basis: same lanes, same Q, noise scaled by 1/d with no rounding term. No level is consumed, so no prime is ever dropped and 'primes after switch' has no referent. Repairing this test would reintroduce the level ladder. See docs/RETIRED_MECHANISMS.md
